Vendored code notice
=====================

The files in this directory (audio_io.py, configuration_moss_audio.py,
modeling_moss_audio.py, processing_moss_audio.py) are copied, mostly
verbatim, from:

  Source:  https://github.com/OpenMOSS/MOSS-Audio
  Path:    src/
  Commit:  5cbb1d823937cd5b5de3d8fa4d3a7253ebd3b883
  Fetched: 2026-08-06

Why vendored instead of depended on: MOSS-Audio's checkpoints on Hugging
Face declare `trust_remote_code` support in config.json for AutoConfig and
AutoProcessor only, not for AutoModel -- there is no modeling code bundled
in the model repo itself, so `AutoModel.from_pretrained(..., trust_remote_code=True)`
fails with "Unrecognized configuration class". The upstream repo's own
`infer.py` works around this by importing `MossAudioModel` directly from its
`src/` package instead of going through transformers' Auto* classes, which
is what these vendored files let this ComfyUI package do too.

`pip install`ing the upstream `moss-audio` package directly was tried and
rejected: its `pyproject.toml` declares `gradio` and `streamlit` (used only
by its own demo `app.py`) as unconditional base dependencies, and pulling
them in force-upgraded `huggingface_hub` to a 1.x release incompatible with
the `transformers` version ComfyUI itself depends on, breaking ComfyUI's own
model loading. Vendoring just the four inference-path files avoids that
entire dependency tree.

License
-------

The upstream repository's own pyproject.toml declares
`license = { file = "LICENSE" }`, and its README states "Models in MOSS-Audio
are licensed under the Apache License 2.0" -- but as of the commit above, no
LICENSE file actually exists in the repository. Apache-2.0 is the clear
intent (matching both the pyproject.toml declaration and the license used by
the model weights), so these files are treated as Apache-2.0 licensed and
redistributed under the terms in LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.txt in this directory,
with copyright retained by the original authors (OpenMOSS Team / MOSI.AI).

Modifications from upstream
----------------------------

Per Apache License 2.0 section 4(b), files changed from the original are
noted here:

- modeling_moss_audio.py: changed `from src.configuration_moss_audio import
  ...` to `from .configuration_moss_audio import ...` (a relative import),
  so the module resolves inside this vendored package
  (boo-moss-audio/vendor/moss_audio/) instead of requiring a top-level `src`
  package on sys.path. No other changes.

All other files are unmodified copies of the upstream source.
